vintermann wrote:
> On Jul 4, 3:29 pm, Derek Ray <moot@just_a_spamtrap_anyway.com> wrote:
> 
>> Why should improving the utility of Cure Blindness take priority over
>> improving the utility of Detect Foot, Invisibility, Levitation, or
>> similar -- the first of which is simply directly useless, and the other
>> two are also rendered less useful by easily-obtainable items in the game?
> 
> You're right. Detect foot is definitively the most useless spell in
> the game. Oh, wait...

It's not about which is more useless and fixing the most useless first.
 It's about providing proper support for your claim that something was
useless in the first place.

> But who cares about "priority"? If someone want to fix things, let
> them do it in the order they like, I say.

_That_ is how you wreck game balance.  It's the difference between a
good patch and a bad patch.  For example, if you nerf unicorn horns
arbitrarily, you make Cure Blindness and carrots better.  Yay.  But do
you make the disease-throwing monsters sufficiently more dangerous that
you break the game in the other direction?  Is the problem actually
unicorn horns, or that blindness isn't even that big of a crippling
defect to begin with?

I am certain he hasn't even considered these things, and that was why I
challenged him; the game is sufficiently complex that making changes
off-the-cuff without thinking them through is NEVER a good idea.

> Nethack is a very varied game. By that I mean that two games probably
> won't look all that much like each other.

Actually, that's not true.  Right now, most ascensions look remarkably
similar beyond a certain point, and in many cases, ascensions look
remarkably similar from the word "go", the only difference being what
levels things were found on.

The deaths are wide and varied.  But the deaths aren't really anything
that needs rebalancing, now, are they?

> variety, and I for one will listen to good YANIs - and maybe even
> write up a patch, if I feel like it.

I'll listen to good YANIs too.  That one wasn't.

As far as writing up patches, I have 150k worth of changes and patches
to the game currently in beta test on a closed server.  If things
continue to go well, I will make the server public in the near future.
I have already been considering whether unicorn horns need "fixing", and
so far I haven't come up with a good reason why they _need_ it, or a
good change that doesn't sufficiently disrupt the game in other aspects.
 That isn't to say that they couldn't be improved to enhance variety,
but it does mean that I'm more interested in hearing well-thought-out
ideas rather than off-the-cuff five-minute specials.

